ollow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the perimeter of the regular hexagon.\n2. Since the octagon has the same perimeter as the hexagon, we can use this perimeter to find the side length of the octagon.\n\nA regular hexagon has 6 sides, so its perimeter is \\(6 \\times 16 = 96\\) cm. A regular octagon has 8 sides, so if we let the side length of the octagon be \\(s\\), then its perimeter is \\(8s\\). Since the perimeters are equal, we have:\n\\[8s = 96\\]\nSolving for \\(s\\), we get:\n\\[s = \\frac{96}{8} = 12\\]\n\nSo, the side length of the octagon is 12 cm. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given side length of the hexagon\nside_length_hexagon = 16\n\n# Number of sides in a hexagon\nnum_sides_hexagon = 6\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = side_length_hexagon * num_sides_hexagon\n\n# Number of sides in an octagon\nnum_sides_octagon = 8\n\n# Calculate the side length of the octagon\nside_length_octagon = perimeter_hexagon / num_sides_octagon\nprint(side_length_octagon)\n```\n```output\n12.0\n```\nThe side length of the regular octagon is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cm.", "To solve this problem, we need to find the side length of a regular octagon that has the same perimeter as a regular hexagon with a side length of 16 cm.\n\n1. First, we calculate the perimeter of the hexagon. Since a hexagon has 6 sides, the perimeter of the hexagon is \\(6 \\times 16 = 96\\) cm.\n2. Next, we know that the perimeter of the octagon is the same as the perimeter of the hexagon, so the perimeter of the octagon is also 96 cm.\n3. Since an octagon has 8 sides, the side length of the octagon can be found by dividing the perimeter of the octagon by 8. So, the side length of the octagon is \\( \\frac{96}{8} = 12 \\) cm.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given side length of the hexagon\nside_length_hexagon = 16\n\n# Number of sides of the hexagon\nnum_sides_hexagon = 6\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = side_length_hexagon * num_sides_hexagon\n\n# Number of sides of the octagon\nnum_sides_octagon = 8\n\n# Calculate the side length of the octagon\nside_length_octagon = perimeter_hexagon / num_sides_octagon\nprint(side_length_octagon)\n```\n```output\n12.0\n```\nThe side length of each side of the octagon is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cm.", "To find the side length of the regular octagon, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the perimeter of the regular hexagon.\n2. Since the octagon has the same perimeter as the hexagon, use the perimeter to find the side length of the octagon.\n\nLet's start by calculating the perimeter of the regular hexagon. A regular hexagon has 6 sides, and each side is 16 cm long. Therefore, the perimeter \\( P \\) of the hexagon is:\n\\[ P = 6 \\times 16 \\text{ cm} = 96 \\text{ cm} \\]\n\nSince the octagon has the same perimeter, the perimeter of the octagon is also 96 cm. A regular octagon has 8 sides. Let \\( s \\) be the side length of the octagon. The perimeter of the octagon can be expressed as:\n\\[ 8s = 96 \\text{ cm} \\]\n\nWe can solve for \\( s \\) by dividing both sides of the equation by 8:\n\\[ s = \\frac{96}{8} \\text{ cm} = 12 \\text{ cm} \\]\n\nSo, the side length of the octagon is 12 cm. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given side length of the hexagon\nside_length_hexagon = 16\n\n# Number of sides of the hexagon\nnum_sides_hexagon = 6\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = side_length_hexagon * num_sides_hexagon\n\n# Number of sides of the octagon\nnum_sides_octagon = 8\n\n# Calculate the side length of the octagon\nside_length_octagon = perimeter_hexagon / num_sides_octagon\nprint(side_length_octagon)\n```\n```output\n12.0\n```\nThe side length of the regular octagon is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cm.", "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the perimeter of the regular hexagon.\n2. Since the regular octagon has the same perimeter as the hexagon, we can use 