 to ensure it holds true. Let\'s do this using Python code to confirm our result.\n```python\n# Define the value of x\nx = 83\n\n# Calculate the left side of the equation: (1/2) * (3x - 9)\nleft_side = (1/2) * (3 * x - 9)\n\n# Calculate the right side of the equation: x + 37\nright_side = x + 37\n\n# Check if both sides are equal\nprint((left_side, right_side, left_side == right_side))\n```\n```output\n(120.0, 120, True)\n```\nThe left side of the equation \\(\\frac{1}{2}(3x - 9)\\) evaluates to 120, and the right side \\(x + 37\\) also evaluates to 120. Since both sides are equal, our solution \\(x = 83\\) is correct.\n\nThus, the value of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{83}\\).', 'To solve the problem, we need to translate the given statement into an algebraic equation and then solve for \\(x\\).\n\nThe statement "Half the value of \\(3x - 9\\) is \\(x + 37\\)" can be written as:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2}(3x - 9) = x + 37\n\\]\n\nWe can solve this equation step-by-step.\n\n1. First, eliminate the fraction by multiplying both sides of the equation by 2:\n\\[\n3x - 9 = 2(x + 37)\n\\]\n\n2. Distribute the 2 on the right side:\n\\[\n3x - 9 = 2x + 74\n\\]\n\n3. Subtract \\(2x\\) from both sides to isolate \\(x\\) on one side:\n\\[\n3x - 2x - 9 = 74\n\\]\n\\[\nx - 9 = 74\n\\]\n\n4. Add 9 to both sides to solve for \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = 74 + 9\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 83\n\\]\n\nLet\'s verify this solution by substituting \\(x = 83\\) back into the original equation to ensure it holds true. We\'ll use Python to confirm the result.\n```python\n# Define the value of x\nx = 83\n\n# Calculate the left side of the equation: half of (3x - 9)\nleft_side = (3 * x - 9) / 2\n\n# Calculate the right side of the equation: x + 37\nright_side = x + 37\n\n# Check if both sides are equal\nprint((left_side, right_side, left_side == right_side))\n```\n```output\n(120.0, 120, True)\n```\nThe left side of the equation evaluates to 120, and the right side also evaluates to 120, confirming that the equation holds true whe