72\\alpha^2 + 88\\alpha - 23)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha^9 = (3\\alpha^2 - 4\\alpha + 1)(9\\alpha^2 - 20\\alpha + 4)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha^9 = 27\\alpha^4 - 60\\alpha^3 + 12\\alpha^2 - 36\\alpha^3 + 80\\alpha^2 - 16\\alpha + 9\\alpha^2 - 20\\alpha + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha^9 = 27\\alpha^4 - 96\\alpha^3 + 101\\alpha^2 - 36\\alpha + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha^9 = 27\\alpha(3\\alpha^2 - 4\\alpha + 1) - 96(3\\alpha^2 - 4\\alpha + 1) + 101\\alpha^2 - 36\\alpha + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha^9 = 81\\alpha^3 - 108\\alpha^2 + 27\\alpha - 288\\alpha^2 + 384\\alpha - 96 + 101\\alpha^2 - 36\\alpha + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha^9 = 81(3\\alpha^2 - 4\\alpha + 1) - 288\\alpha^2 + 384\\alpha - 96 + 101\\alpha^2 - 36\\alpha + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha^9 = 243\\alpha^2 - 324\\alpha + 81 - 288\\alpha^2 + 384\\alpha - 96 + 101\\alpha^2 - 36\\alpha + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha^9 = 56\\alpha^2 + 24\\alpha - 11\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\\[\n\\alpha^9 + p\\alpha^6 + q\\alpha^3 + r = 56\\alpha^2 + 24\\alpha - 11 + p(9\\alpha^4 - 24\\alpha^3 + 18\\alpha^2 - 8\\alpha + 1) + q(3\\alpha^2 - 4\\alpha + 1) + r = 0\n\\]\n\nBy comparing the coefficients of \\(\\alpha^2, \\alpha, \\text{and the constant term}\\), we get:\n\\[\n56 + 18p + 3q = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n24 - 8p - 4q = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n-11 + p + q + r = 0\n\\]\n\nSolving these equations, we get:\n\\[\n24 - 8p - 4q = 0 \\implies 6 - 2p - q = 0 \\implies q = 6 - 2p\n\\]\n\\[\n56 + 18p + 3q = 0 \\implies 56 + 18p + 3(6 - 2p) = 0 \\implies 56 + 18p + 18 - 6p = 0 \\implies 74 + 12p = 0 \\implies p = -\\frac{37}{6}\n\\]\n\\[\nq = 6 - 2\\left(-\\frac{37}{6}\\right) = 6 + \\frac{37}{3} = \\frac{55}{3}\n\\]\n\\[\n-11 + p + q + r = 0 \\implies -11 - \\frac{37}{6} + \\frac{55}{3} + r = 0 \\implies -11 - \\frac{37}{6} + \\frac{110}{6} + r = 0 \\implies \\frac{-66 - 37 + 110}{6} + r = 0 \\implies \\frac{7}{6} + r = 0 \\implies r = -\\frac{7}{6}\n\\]\n\nSo, the ordered triple \\((p, q, r)\\) is:\n\\[\n\\left(-\\frac{37}{6}, \\frac{55}{3}, -\\frac{7}{6}\\right)\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python to ensure the 