c{\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\cot x\n\\]\n\nSo the simplified expression is \\(\\cot x\\). Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, sec, sin, cos, simplify, cot\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nx = symbols('x')\r\n\r\n# Define the expression\r\nexpression = sec(x) / sin(x) - sin(x) / cos(x)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expression = simplify(expression)\r\n\r\n# Print the simplified expression\r\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```\n```output\n1/tan(x)\n```\nThe simplified expression is \\(\\frac{1}{\\tan x}\\), which is equivalent to \\(\\cot x\\). Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\cot x}\n\\]", "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Recall that \\(\\sec x = \\frac{1}{\\cos x}\\).\n2. Substitute \\(\\sec x\\) with \\(\\frac{1}{\\cos x}\\) in the expression.\n3. Simplify the resulting expression by finding a common denominator and combining the fractions.\n\nLet's do this step-by-step.\n\n1. Substitute \\(\\sec x\\) with \\(\\frac{1}{\\cos x}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{\\cos x}}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}.\n\\]\n\n2. Simplify the first term:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\cos x}}{\\sin x} = \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x}.\n\\]\n\n3. Now we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}.\n\\]\n\n4. To combine these fractions, we need a common denominator. The common denominator is \\(\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x \\cdot \\sin x}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} = \\frac{1 - \\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x}.\n\\]\n\n5. Recall the Pythagorean identity: \\(1 - \\sin^2 x = \\cos^2 x\\). So we can substitute this in:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\cos^2 x}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\cot x.\n\\]\n\nSo the simplified expression is \\(\\cot x\\). Let's confirm this using Python code.\n```python\