ec x\\) with \\(\\frac{1}{\\cos x}\\) in the expression.\n3. Simplify the resulting expression.\n\nLet's break it down step by step:\n\n1. Substitute \\(\\sec x\\) with \\(\\frac{1}{\\cos x}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{\\cos x}}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}.\n   \\]\n\n2. Combine the terms over a common denominator:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} = \\frac{1 - \\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x}.\n   \\]\n\n3. Use the Pythagorean identity \\(1 - \\sin^2 x = \\cos^2 x\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1 - \\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} = \\frac{\\cos^2 x}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\cot x.\n   \\]\n\nSo the simplified expression is \\(\\cot x\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code using sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nx = sp.symbols('x')\n\n# Define the expression\nexpr = sp.sec(x) / sp.sin(x) - sp.sin(x) / sp.cos(x)\n\n# Simplify the expression\nsimplified_expr = sp.simplify(expr)\nprint(simplified_expr)\n```\n```output\n1/tan(x)\n```\nThe output from the code confirms our manual simplification. The expression \\(\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\) simplifies to \\(\\cot x\\), which is equivalent to \\(\\frac{1}{\\tan x}\\).\n\nTherefore, the simplified expression is \\(\\boxed{\\cot x}\\).", "To solve the given expression \\(\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\), let's first express \\(\\sec x\\) in terms of \\(\\cos x\\). We know that \\(\\sec x = \\frac{1}{\\cos x}\\). So, we can rewrite the expression as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{\\cos x}}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we need a common den