c \\), the trisectors divide these angles into three equal parts of \\( 25^\\circ \\) each.\n\nTo find \\( \\angle AFD \\), we need to consider the angles around point \\( F \\):\n- \\( \\angle AFD \\) is the external angle to the triangle formed by the trisectors.\n\nUsing the properties of the trisectors and the angles in the quadrilateral, we can determine that:\n\\[\n\\angle AFD = 180^\\circ - (\\angle BAF + \\angle DAF)\n\\]\n\nSince \\( \\angle BAF \\) and \\( \\angle DAF \\) are each \\( 25^\\circ \\):\n\\[\n\\angle AFD = 180^\\circ - (25^\\circ + 25^\\circ)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\angle AFD = 180^\\circ - 50^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n\\angle AFD = 130^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the degree measure of angle \\( \\angle AFD \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{130^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nTo ensure the accuracy, let's verify the calculations using Python.\n```python\n# Given angles and trisected angles\nangle_BAD = 3 * 25  # 75 degrees\nangle_CDA = 3 * 25  # 75 degrees\n\n# The trisected angles\ntrisected_angle_BAD = 25  # degrees\ntrisected_angle_CDA = 25  # degrees\n\n# Calculate angle AFD\nangle_AFD = 180 - (trisected_angle_BAD + trisected_angle_CDA)\nprint(angle_AFD)\n```", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the measure of angle \\( \\angle AFD \\) in the quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\) where angles \\( \\angle BAD \\) and \\( \\angle CDA \\) are trisected.\n\nGiven:\n- \\( \\angle BAD = 110^\\circ \\)\n- \\( \\angle CDA = 100^\\circ \\)\n\nSince \\( \\angle BAD \\) is trisected, each of the smaller angles is \\( \\frac{110^\\circ}{3} \\).\nSince \\( \\angle CDA \\) is trisected, each of the smaller angles is \\( \\frac{100^\\circ}{3} \\).\n\nLet's denote the trisected angles as follows:\n- \\( \\angle BAE = \\angle EAF = \\angle FAD = \\frac{110^\\circ}{3} \\)\n- \\( \\angle ADE = \\angle EDF = \\angle FDC = \\frac{100^\\circ}{3} \\)\n\nWe need to find the measure of \\( \\angle AFD \\). To do this, we can use the fact that the sum of the angles around point \\( F \\) is \\( 360^\\circ \\).\n\nThe angles around point \\( F \\) are:\n- \\( \\angle AFD \\)\n- \\( \\angle AFE \\)\n- \\( \\angle EFD \\)\n\nSince \\( \\angle AFE \\) and \\( \\angle EFD \\) are part of the trisected angles, we have:\n- \\( \\angle AFE = \\frac{110^\\circ}{3} \\)\n- \\( \\angle EFD = \\frac{100^\\circ}{3} \\)\n\nThe sum of these angles around point \\( F \\) is:\n\\[ \\angle AFD + \\angle AFE + \\angle EFD = 180^\\circ \\]\n\\[ \\angle AFD + \\frac{110^\\circ}{3} + \\frac{100^\\circ}{3} = 180^\\circ \\]\n\\[ \\angle AFD + \\frac{210^\\circ}{3} = 180^\\circ \\]\n\\[ \\angle AFD + 70^\\circ = 180^\\circ \\]\n\\[ \\angle AFD = 180^\\circ - 70^\\circ \\]\n\\[ \\angle AFD = 110^\\circ \\]\n\nThus, the measure of angle \\( \\angle AFD \\) is \\( 110^\\circ \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Calculation of the angle AFD\r\nangle_BAD = 110\r\nangle_CDA = 100\r\n\r\n# Trisected angles\r\nangle_BAE = angle_EAF = angle_FAD = angle_BAD / 3\r\nangle_ADE = angle_EDF = angle_FDC = angle_CDA / 3\r\n\r\n# Sum of angles around point F\r\nangle_AFD = 180 - (angle_BAE + angle_EDF)\r\n\r\nprint(angle_AFD)\n```\n```output\n110.0\n```\nThe measure of angle \\( \\angle AFD \\) is \\(\\boxed{110^\\circ}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to use the properties of the angles in the quadrilateral and the trisected angles. Here are the steps to find the measure of angle \\( \\angle AFD \\):\n\n1. First, let's denote the trisected angles as follows:\n   - \\( \\angle BAD = 3x \\)\n   - \\( \\angle CDA = 3y \\)\n\n2. Since \\( \\angle BAD \\) and \\( \\angle CDA \\) are trisected, we have:\n   - \\( \\angle BAE = \\angle EAF = \\angle FAD = x \\)\n   - \\( \\angle ADE = \\angle EDF = \\angle FDC = y \\)\n\n3. The sum of the interior angles of quadrilateral \\( ABCD \\) is \\( 360^\\circ \\). Therefore:\n   \\[\n   \\angle BAD + \\angle ABC + \\angle BCD + \\angle CDA = 360^\\circ\n   \\]\n   Substituting the trisected angles, we get:\n   \\[\n   3x + \\angle ABC + \\angle