ta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\sin 5^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ}.\n   \\]\n   This can be simplified further by recognizing that:\n   \\[\n   \\cos 25^\\circ = \\sin 65^\\circ \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\sin 5^\\circ = \\cos 85^\\circ.\n   \\]\n   Therefore, we can use the tangent addition formula:\n   \\[\n   \\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\sin 65^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ} = \\frac{\\sin 65^\\circ + \\sin 5^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ}.\n   \\]\n   Using the identity \\(\\sin 65^\\circ = \\cos 25^\\circ\\), we get:\n   \\[\n   \\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\sin 5^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ}.\n   \\]\n   This can be simplified to:\n   \\[\n   \\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\sin 5^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ} = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ} = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ}{-\\cos 65^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ} = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ}{-\\cos (90^\\circ - 25^\\circ) - \\cos 5^\\circ} = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ}{-\\sin 25^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ}.\n   \\", "To solve the problem, we need to simplify the given expression for $\\tan \\theta$ and find the angle $\\theta$. Let's break it down step-by-step.\n\n1. **Simplify the Numerator and Denominator:**\n   The numerator of the given expression is:\n   \\[\n   \\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ\n   \\]\n   The denominator of the given expression is:\n   \\[\n   \\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n2. **Use Trigonometric Identities:**\n   We can use the product-to-sum identities and angle addition/subtraction identities to simplify the expressions.\n\n   The numerator can be simplified using the identity:\n   \\[\n   \\cos A \\cos B 