\sin(25^\\circ) - \\sin(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n-\\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ = -\\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(85^\\circ) + \\sin(-15^\\circ)] = -\\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(85^\\circ) - \\sin(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(25^\\circ) - \\sin(-15^\\circ)] = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(25^\\circ) + \\sin(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n-\\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ = -\\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(85^\\circ) - \\sin(-15^\\circ)] = -\\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(85^\\circ) + \\sin(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\nCombining these, the denominator becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(25^\\circ) - \\sin(15^\\circ) - \\sin(85^\\circ) + \\sin(15^\\circ) + \\sin(25^\\circ) + \\sin(15^\\circ) - \\sin(85^\\circ) - \\sin(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} [2\\sin(25^\\circ) - 2\\sin(85^\\circ)] = \\sin(25^\\circ) - \\sin(85^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos(25^\\circ) + \\cos(85^\\circ)}{\\sin(25^\\circ) - \\sin(85^\\circ)}\n\\]\n\nUsing the sum-to-product identities:\n\\[\n\\cos(25^\\circ) + \\cos(85^\\circ) = 2 \\cos\\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\cos\\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos(55^\\circ) \\cos(-30^\\circ) = 2 \\cos(55^\\circ) \\cos(30^\\circ)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin(25^\\circ) - \\sin(85^\\circ) = 2 \\cos\\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\sin\\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos(55^\\circ) \\sin(-30^\\circ) = -2 \\cos(55^\\circ) \\sin(30^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{2 \\cos(55^\\circ) \\cos(30^\\circ)}{-2 \\cos(55^\\circ) \\sin(30^\\circ)} = \\frac{\\cos(30^\\circ)}{-\\sin(30^\\circ)} = -\\cot(30^\\circ) = -\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\tan \\theta = -\\sqrt{3}\\), the least positive angle \\(\\theta\\) is \\(150^\\circ\\).\n\nFinally, let's verify this using Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the value of tan(theta)\nnumerator = math.cos(math.radians(25)) + math.cos(math.radians(85))\ndenominator = math.sin(math.radians(25)) - math.sin(math.