2k + 1 \\) for some integer \\( k \\).\n\nNext, we need to find \\( k \\) such that \\( 12k + 1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{7} \\). This simplifies to \\( 12k \\equiv -1 \\pmod{7} \\). Since \\( 12 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7} \\), this becomes \\( 5k \\equiv -1 \\pmod{7} \\). We can find the multiplicative inverse of 5 modulo 7, which is 3 (since \\( 5 \\times 3 = 15 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7} \\)). So, \\( k \\equiv -1 \\times 3 \\pmod{7} \\equiv -3 \\pmod{7} \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7} \\). Therefore, \\( k = 7m + 4 \\) for some integer \\( m \\).\n\nSubstituting \\( k = 7m + 4 \\) into \\( x = 12k + 1 \\), we get \\( x = 12(7m + 4) + 1 = 84m + 49 \\). Since \\( x < 75 \\), we need \\( 84m + 49 < 75 \\). This simplifies to \\( 84m < 26 \\), so \\( m = 0 \\). Therefore, \\( x = 49 \\).\n\nSo, Rosa's age is 49. Let's verify this using Python code to ensure the result is accurate.\n```python\n# Function to check if a number satisfies all the given conditions\ndef check_age(age):\n    return (age % 2 == 1 and age % 3 == 1 and age % 4 == 1 and age % 6 == 1 and age % 7 == 0 and age < 75)\n\n# Iterate through possible ages to find the correct one\nfor age in range(1, 75):\n    if check_age(age):\n        rosa_age = age\n        break\n\nprint(rosa_age)\n```\n```output\n49\n```\nThe code confirms that Rosa's age is \\(\\boxed{49}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to find a number \\( x \\) that satisfies the following conditions:\n1. \\( x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{2} \\)\n2. \\( x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\)\n3. \\( x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4} \\)\n4. \\( x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6} \\)\n5. \\( x \\equiv 0 \\pmod{7} \\)\n6. \\( x < 75 \\)\n\nFirst, we note that conditions 1, 2, 3, and 4 can be combined into a single condition because the least common multiple (LCM) of 2, 3, 4, and 6 is 12. So, we can rewrite the conditions as:\n1. \\( x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{12} \\)\n2. \\( x \\equiv 0 \\pmod{7} \\)\n3. \\( x < 75 \\)\n\nThis means \\( x = 12k + 1 \\) for some integer \\( k \\), and \\( x = 7m \\) for some integer \\( m \\). So w