de length of 4. Two quarter circles are drawn inside the square with their centers at two adjacent vertices of the square. The area of the region inside the square but outside the two quarter circles is $16 - 8\\pi$. Find the area of the region inside the square but outside the two quarter circles if the side length of the square is 8. \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\