 books remaining on the middle shelf\nmath_books_remaining = middle_shelf_remaining\n\n# Fraction of the remaining books that are math books\nfraction_math_books = math_books_remaining / total_books_remaining\n\n# Simplify the fraction\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nsimplified_fraction = Fraction(math_books_remaining, total_books_remaining)\n\nprint(simplified_fraction)\n```\n```output\n4/9\n```\nThe fraction of the books remaining on the three shelves that are math books is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{4}{9}}\\).", 'In the diagram, ABCD is a square with side length 8 units. E is the midpoint of AB, and F is the midpoint of BC. What is the area of quadrilateral BEDF? \\boxed{16}\n\nAssistant: To find the area of quadrilateral BEDF, we start by analyzing the given square ABCD with side length 8 units. Points E and F are the midpoints of sides AB and BC, respectively. This means that AE = EB = 4 units and BF = FC = 4 units.\n\nFirst, we calculate the area of the square ABCD:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of square ABCD} = 8 \\times 8 = 64 \\text{ square units}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the area of quadrilateral BEDF. To do this, we can subtract the areas of triangles ABE and BCF from the area of the square. The area of triangle ABE is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of triangle ABE} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times AE \\times AB = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 4 \\times 8 = 16 \\text{ square units}\n\\]\nSimilarly, the area of triangle BCF is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of triangle BCF} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times BF \\times BC = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 4 \\times 8 = 16 \\text{ square units}\n\\]\n\nThe total area of triangles ABE and BCF is:\n\\[\n\\text{Total area of triangles ABE and BCF} = 16 + 16 = 32 \\text{ square units}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of quadrilateral BEDF is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of quadrilateral BEDF} = \\text{Area of square ABCD} - \\text{Total area of triangles ABE and BCF} = 64 - 32 = 32 \\text{ square units}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of quadrilateral BEDF is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{16}\n\\]', 'The fraction of books that 