xpression. Let's simplify the expression step by step.\n\nThe expression given is:\n\\[ \\left(-\\frac{7}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{2}\\right) \\left(\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{2}\\right) \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{2} - \\frac{7}{2}\\right) \\left(\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{2}\\right) \\]\n\nWe can pair the terms and simplify them:\n\\[ \\left(-\\frac{7}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{2}\\right) \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{2} - \\frac{7}{2}\\right) \\left(\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{2}\\right) \\left(\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{2}\\right) \\]\n\nEach pair can be simplified using the difference of squares formula:\n\\[ \\left(-\\frac{7}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{2}\\right) \\left(-\\frac{7}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{2}\\right) = \\left(-\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2 - \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{49}{4} - \\frac{29}{4} = \\frac{20}{4} = 5 \\]\n\\[ \\left(\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{2}\\right) \\left(\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{2}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2 - \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{9}{4} - \\frac{29}{4} = \\frac{-20}{4} = -5 \\]\n\nSo the product of the \\( y \\)-coordinates is:\n\\[ 5 \\cdot (-5) = -25 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this by simplifying the expression using SymPy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define variables\nx, y = sp.symbols('x y')\n\n# Define the equations\neq1 = y - (x**2 - 8)\neq2 = y**2 - (-5*x + 44)\n\n# Substitute y = x^2 - 8 into y^2 = -5x + 44\nsubstituted_eq = eq2.subs(y, x**2 - 8)\n\n# Solve for x\nx_solutions = sp.solve(substituted_eq, x)\n\n# Find the corresponding y-coordinates\ny_solutions = [x_val**2 - 8 for x_val in x_solutions]\n\n# Calculate the product of the y-coordinates\nproduct_of_y_coords = sp.prod(y_solutions)\n\n# Simplify the product of the y-coordinates\nsimplified_product = sp.simplify(product_of_y_coords)\n\n# Print the simplified product of the y-coordinates\nprint(simplified_product)\n```\n```output\n-25\n```\nThe simplified product of the \\( y