l number of students \\( S \\), we need to isolate \\( S \\). We can do this by multiplying both sides of the equation by the reciprocal of \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\), which is \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\):\n\\[\nS = 834 \\times \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nNow, let's perform the multiplication:\n\\[\nS = 834 \\times \\frac{3}{2} = 834 \\times 1.5\n\\]\n\nTo simplify the multiplication:\n\\[\n834 \\times 1.5 = 834 \\times \\left(1 + 0.5\\right) = 834 \\times 1 + 834 \\times 0.5\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term separately:\n\\[\n834 \\times 1 = 834\n\\]\n\\[\n834 \\times 0.5 = 417\n\\]\n\nAdd the results together:\n\\[\n834 + 417 = 1251\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of students at Baker Middle School is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1251}\n\\]\n\nMultiply the following two matrices:\n$\\left(\n\\begin{array}{cccc}\n2 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\\n-1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)$ and\n$\\left(\n\\begin{array}{cccc}\n-3 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\\n-1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\\n1 & -3 & 0 & -2 \\\\\n2 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)$.\nTo multiply the two matrices, we need to take the dot product of each row of the first matrix with each column of the second matrix. Let's go through this step by step.\n\nThe first matrix is:\n\\[\nA = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{cccc}\n2 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\\n-1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)\n\\]\nand the second matrix is:\n\\[\nB = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{cccc}\n-3 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\\n-1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\\n1 & -3 & 0 & -2 \\\\\n2 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)\n\\]\n\nThe product matrix \\( C = AB \\) will be a 2x4 matrix. Let's calculate each element of \\( C \\).\n\nThe element in the first row and first column of \\( C \\) is:\n\\[\nC_{11} = 2 \\cdot (-3) + 0 \\cdot (-1) + 1 \\cdot 1 + (-1) \\cdot 2 = -6 + 0 + 1 - 2 = -7\n\\]\n\nThe element in the first row and second column of \\( C \\) is:\n\\[\nC_{12} = 2 \\cdot 1 + 0 \\cdot 2 + 1 \\cdot (-3) + (-1) \\cdot (-1) = 2 + 0 - 3 + 1 = 0\n\\]\n\nThe element in the first row and third column of \\( C \\) is:\n\\[\nC_{13} = 2 \\cdot 3 + 0 \\cdot (-2) + 1 \\cdot 0 + (-1) \\cdot 1 = 6 + 0 + 0 - 1 = 5\n\\]\n\nThe element in the first row and fourth column of \\( C \\) is:\n\\[\nC_{14} = 2 \\cdot (-2) + 0 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot (-2) + (-1) \\cdot 1 = -4 + 0 - 2 - 1 = -7\n\\]\n\nThe element in the second row and first column of \\( C \\) is:\n\\[\nC_{21} = -1 \\cdot (-3) + (-2) \\cdot (-1) + 1 \\cdot 1 + 2 \\cdot 2 = 3 + 2 + 1 + 4 = 10\n\\]\n\nThe element in the second row and second column of \\( C \\) is:\n\\[\nC_{22} = -1 \\cdot 1 + (-2) \\cdot 2 + 1 \\cdot (-3) + 2 \\cdot (-1) = -1 - 4 - 3 - 2 = -10\n\\]\n\nThe element in the second row and third column of \\( C \\) is:\n\\[\nC_{23} = -1 \\cdot 3 + (-2) \\cdot (-2) + 1 \\cdot 0 + 2 \\cdot 1 = -3 + 4 + 0 + 2 = 3\n\\]\n\nThe element in the second row and fourth column of \\( C \\) is:\n\\[\nC_{24} = -1 \\cdot (-2) + (-2) \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot (-2) + 2 \\cdot 1 = 2 - 2 - 2 + 2 = 0\n\\]\n\nPutting it all together, the product matrix \\( C \\) is:\n\\[\nC = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{cccc}\n-7 & 0 & 5 & -7 \\\\\n10 & -10 & 3 & 0 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)\n\\]\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\left(\n\\begin{array}{cccc}\n-7 & 0 & 5 & -7 \\\\\n10 & -10 & 3 & 0 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)}\n\\]", "To find the total number of students at Baker Middle School, we can set up an equation based on the information given. Let's denote the total number of students by \\( x \\). According to the problem, two-thirds of the students take music, and this number is given as 834. So we can write the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{2}{3} x = 834\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\( x \\), we need to isolate \\( x \\) on one side of the equation. We can do this by multiplying both sides of the equation by the reciprocal of \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\), which is \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\):\n\n\\[\nx = 834 \\times \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nNow we can compute the value of \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\nx = 834 \\times \\frac{3}{2} = \\frac{834 \\times 3}{2} = \\frac{2502}{2} = 1251\n\\]\n\nSo the total n