 -4 \\).\n\nTherefore, the function \\( f(x) \\) is undefined at \\( x = -4 \\). The domain of \\( f(x) \\) is all real numbers except \\( x = -4 \\).\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{(-\\infty, -4) \\cup (-4, \\infty)} \\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python code.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\r\n\r\n# Define the variable and the expressions\r\nx = sp.symbols('x')\r\nexpr1 = x**2 + 3*x - 4\r\nexpr2 = x**2 + 9*x + 20\r\n\r\n# Solve for the roots of the expressions\r\nroots_expr1 = sp.solve(expr1, x)\r\nroots_expr2 = sp.solve(expr2, x)\r\n\r\n# Find the common roots\r\ncommon_roots = set(roots_expr1).intersection(set(roots_expr2))\r\n\r\nprint((roots_expr1, roots_expr2, common_roots))\n```", 'Express your answer as an interval or as a union of intervals. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{