ode to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given angle\nangle_given = 128\n\n# Calculate the angle QPT which is supplementary to the given angle\nangle_QPT = 180 - angle_given\n\n# Since angle QPT is 3x, we can find x\nx = angle_QPT / 3\n\n# The measure of angle PQR is the same as angle QPT\nangle_PQR = angle_QPT\n\nprint((x, angle_PQR))\n```\n```output\n(17.333333333333332, 52)\n```\nThe value of \\(x\\) is approximately \\(17.33^\\circ\\), but the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(52^\\circ\\).\n\nSo, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(\\boxed{52}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to use the properties of parallel lines and angles. Here's the step-by-step reasoning:\n\n1. Since \\(PT\\) is parallel to \\(QR\\), the angle \\(\\angle PQR\\) is equal to the angle \\(\\angle QPT\\) (alternate interior angles).\n\n2. The angle \\(\\angle QPT\\) is composed of two angles: \\(x^\\circ\\) and \\(2x^\\circ\\). Therefore, \\(\\angle QPT = x^\\circ + 2x^\\circ = 3x^\\circ\\).\n\n3. Since \\(\\angle PQR = \\angle QPT\\), we have \\(\\angle PQR = 3x^\\circ\\).\n\n4. The angle \\(\\angle QRT\\) is given as \\(128^\\circ\\). Since \\(PT\\) is parallel to \\(QR\\), the angle \\(\\angle QRT\\) is supplementary to \\(\\angle PQR\\). This means that \\(\\angle PQR + \\angle QRT = 180^\\circ\\).\n\n5. Substituting the values, we get \\(3x + 128 = 180\\). Solving for \\(x\\), we get:\n   \\[\n   3x = 180 - 128\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3x = 52\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{52}{3}\n   \\]\n\n6. Since \\(\\angle PQR = 3x\\), we substitute \\(x\\) to find \\(\\angle PQR\\):\n   \\[\n   \\angle PQR = 3 \\left(\\frac{52}{3}\\right) = 52^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(52^\\circ\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Calculation to confirm the angle PQR\n# Given that angle QRT is 128 degrees and angle PQR is 3x\n# We know that 3x + 128 = 180\n# Solving for x\nangle_QRT = 128\nangle_PQR = 180 - angle_QRT\nx = angle_PQR 