\(5 - \\sqrt{3}\\).\n\nTo find the product of \\(5 + \\sqrt{3}\\) and its radical conjugate \\(5 - \\sqrt{3}\\), we can use the difference of squares formula:\n\\[\n(a + \\sqrt{b})(a - \\sqrt{b}) = a^2 - (\\sqrt{b})^2 = a^2 - b.\n\\]\nHere, \\(a = 5\\) and \\(b = 3\\), so the product is:\n\\[\n(5 + \\sqrt{3})(5 - \\sqrt{3}) = 5^2 - (\\sqrt{3})^2 = 25 - 3 = 22.\n\\]\nLet's verify this using Python code.\n```python\n# Define the values\na = 5\nb = 3\n\n# Calculate the product using the difference of squares formula\nproduct = a**2 - b\nprint(product)\n```\n```output\n22\n```\nThe product of \\(5 + \\sqrt{3}\\) and its radical conjugate \\(5 - \\sqrt{3}\\) is \\(\\boxed{22}\\).", "The radical conjugate of $5+\\sqrt{3}$ is $5-\\sqrt{3}$. The product of a number and its radical conjugate is given by the difference of squares formula. Specifically, for a number of the form $a + \\sqrt{b}$, its radical conjugate is $a - \\sqrt{b}$, and their product is $(a + \\sqrt{b})(a - \\sqrt{b}) = a^2 - (\\sqrt{b})^2 = a^2 - b$. \n\nIn this case, the number is $5 + \\sqrt{3}$ and its radical conjugate is $5 - \\sqrt{3}$. So, the product is:\n\n\\[\n(5 + \\sqrt{3})(5 - \\sqrt{3}) = 5^2 - (\\sqrt{3})^2 = 25 - 3 = 22\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this by calculating it in Python.\n```python\n# Define the number and its radical conjugate\nnumber = 5 + (3**0.5)\nconjugate = 5 - (3**0.5)\n\n# Calculate the product\nproduct = number * conjugate\nprint(product)\n```\n```output\n22.0\n```\nThe product of the number $5 + \\sqrt{3}$ and its radical conjugate $5 - \\sqrt{3}$ is \\(\\boxed{22}\\).", "The radical conjugate of a number of the form \\(a + \\sqrt{b}\\) is \\(a - \\sqrt{b}\\). In this case, the radical conjugate of \\(5 + \\sqrt{3}\\) is \\(5 - \\sqrt{3}\\).\n\nTo find the product of \\(5 + \\sqrt{3}\\) and \\(5 - \\sqrt{3}\\), we can use the difference of squares formula:\n\n\\[\n(a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2\n\\]\n\nHere, \\(a = 5\\) and \\(b = \\sqrt{3}\\), so the product is:\n\n\\[\n(5 + \\sq