n, we get:\n\n\\[ 1331 = 11^3 = 11 \\times 11 \\times 11 \\]\n\\[ 9999 = 3^2 \\times 11 \\times 101 = 3 \\times 3 \\times 11 \\times 101 \\]\n\nThe GCD of 1331 and 9999 is 11. So, we can divide both the numerator and the denominator by 11:\n\n\\[ \\frac{1331 \\div 11}{9999 \\div 11} = \\frac{121}{909} \\]\n\nThe fraction \\(\\frac{121}{909}\\) is in its simplest form because the GCD of 121 and 909 is 1. Therefore, \\(a = 121\\) and \\(b = 909\\), and the sum \\(a + b = 121 + 909 = 1030\\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the accuracy.\n```python\nfrom math import gcd\r\n\r\n# Values of the numerator and denominator\r\nnumerator = 1331\r\ndenominator = 9999\r\n\r\n# Calculate the greatest common divisor\r\ncommon_divisor = gcd(numerator, denominator)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the fraction\r\nsimplified_numerator = numerator // common_divisor\r\nsimplified_denominator = denominator // common_divisor\r\n\r\n# Calculate the sum of a and b\r\nresult = simplified_numerator + simplified_denominator\r\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n1030\n```\nThe sum of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) when \\(0.\\overline{1331}\\) is written as a fraction in its simplest form is \\(\\boxed{1030}\\).", "To solve the problem of converting the repeating decimal \\(0.\\overline{1331}\\) into a fraction, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Let \\(x = 0.\\overline{1331}\\).\n2. Then, \\(10000x = 1331.\\overline{1331}\\) (since the repeating part is 4 digits long).\n3. Subtract the original \\(x\\) from this equation: \\(10000x - x = 1331.\\overline{1331} - 0.\\overline{1331}\\).\n4. This simplifies to \\(9999x = 1331\\), so \\(x = \\frac{1331}{9999}\\).\n5. Simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{1331}{9999}\\) by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 1331 and 9999. The GCD of 1331 and 9999 is 11, so \\(\\frac{1331}{9999} = \\frac{121}{909}\\).\n6. Since 121 and 909 have no common divisors other than 1, the fraction \\(\\frac{121}{909}\\) is in its simplest form.\n7. Therefore, \\(a = 121\\) and \\(b = 