's perform these steps:\n\n\\[ 9999 \\div 1331 = 7 \\text{ with remainder } 882 \\]\n\\[ 1331 \\div 882 = 1 \\text{ with remainder } 449 \\]\n\\[ 882 \\div 449 = 1 \\text{ with remainder } 433 \\]\n\\[ 449 \\div 433 = 1 \\text{ with remainder } 16 \\]\n\\[ 433 \\div 16 = 27 \\text{ with remainder } 1 \\]\n\\[ 16 \\div 1 = 16 \\text{ with remainder } 0 \\]\n\nSo, the GCD of 1331 and 9999 is 11. Therefore, we can simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{1331}{9999}\\) by dividing both the numerator and the denominator by 11:\n\n\\[ \\frac{1331 \\div 11}{9999 \\div 11} = \\frac{121}{909} \\]\n\nSince 121 and 909 have no common factors other than 1 (i.e., they are coprime), the fraction \\(\\frac{121}{909}\\) is in its simplest form. Thus, \\(a = 121\\) and \\(b = 909\\), and \\(a + b = 121 + 909 = 1030\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1030}\n\\]\n\nTo verify the accuracy, let's use Python to confirm the steps.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Define the repeating decimal as a fraction\nnumerator = 1331\ndenominator = 9999\n\n# Calculate the greatest common divisor (GCD)\ngcd = math.gcd(numerator, denominator)\n\n# Simplify the fraction\nsimplified_numerator = numerator // gcd\nsimplified_denominator = denominator // gcd\n\n# Calculate the sum of the simplified numerator and denominator\nresult = simplified_numerator + simplified_denominator\nprint(result)\n```", "To convert the repeating decimal $0.\\overline{1331}$ into a fraction, we can use the following method:\n\n1. Let $x = 0.\\overline{1331}$.\n2. Then $10000x = 1331.\\overline{1331}$.\n3. Subtracting the first equation from the second, we get $10000x - x = 1331.\\overline{1331} - 0.\\overline{1331}$.\n4. This simplifies to $9999x = 1331$.\n5. Solving for $x$, we get $x = \\frac{1331}{9999}$.\n\nNow, we need to simplify the fraction $\\frac{1331}{9999}$ to its lowest terms. We can do this by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 1331 and 9999. If the GCD is 1, then the fraction is already in its simplest fo