ing fsolve\nroots = fsolve(equation, initial_guesses)\n\n# Convert the roots to complex numbers\nroots = [complex(root) for root in roots]\n\n# Calculate the area of the polygon formed by the roots\ndef polygon_area(vertices):\n    n = len(vertices)\n    area = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        x1, y1 = vertices[i].real, vertices[i].imag\n        x2, y2 = vertices[(i + 1) % n].real, vertices[(i + 1) % n].imag\n        area += x1 * y2 - y1 * x2\n    return abs(area) / 2\n\narea = polygon_area(roots)\n\n# Print the area\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\nTypeError: can't convert complex to float\n```\nThe error you're encountering is due to the fact that `fsolve` from `scipy.optimize` is not designed to handle complex numbers directly. We need to use a different method to find the roots of the polynomial with complex coefficients. We can use `numpy.roots` which is designed to handle such polynomials.\n\nLet's use `numpy.roots` to find the roots and then calculate the area of the polygon formed by these roots.\n\nHere is the corrected code:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the coefficients of the polynomial\ncoefficients = [1, 4j, -6, -4j, -1j]\n\n# Find the roots of the polynomial\nroots = np.roots(coefficients)\n\n# Calculate the area of the polygon formed by the roots\ndef polygon_area(vertices):\n    n = len(vertices)\n    area = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        x1, y1 = vertices[i].real, vertices[i].imag\n        x2, y2 = vertices[(i + 1) % n].real, vertices[(i + 1) % n].imag\n        area += x1 * y2 - y1 * x2\n    return abs(area) / 2\n\narea = polygon_area(roots)\n\n# Print the area\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n6.0000000000000036\n```\nThe area of the polygon formed by the roots of the polynomial \\(z^4 + 4z^3i - 6z^2 - 4zi - i = 0\\) is approximately \\(6\\). Since the area is given in the form \\(p^{a/b}\\), we need to express \\(6\\) in this form. The simplest way to do this is \\(6 = 6^1\\), where \\(p = 6\\), \\(a = 1\\), and \\(b = 1\\). However