} = 15 \\times 4 = 60 \\text{ cents}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Total cost for Peru} = 6 \\times 4 = 24 \\text{ cents}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Total cost for Spain} = 10 \\times 5 = 50 \\text{ cents}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total cost for all stamps} = 72 + 60 + 24 + 50 = 206 \\text{ cents}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of stamps} = 12 + 15 + 6 + 10 = 43\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average price per stamp} = \\frac{206}{43} \\approx 4.7907 \\text{ cents}\n\\]\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth of a cent, the average price is \\(4.8\\) cents. However, since the choices given are rounded to the nearest tenth, we should check the closest option.\n\nLet's run the Python code to verify these calculations.\n```python\n# Number of stamps from each country in the 1970s\nbrazil_stamps = 12\nfrance_stamps = 15\nperu_stamps = 6\nspain_stamps = 10\n\n# Price per stamp for each country\nbrazil_price = 6\nfrance_price = 4\nperu_price = 4\nspain_price = 5\n\n# Calculate the total cost for each country\ntotal_cost_brazil = brazil_stamps * brazil_price\ntotal_cost_france = france_stamps * france_price\ntotal_cost_peru = peru_stamps * peru_price\ntotal_cost_spain = spain_stamps * spain_price\n\n# Calculate the total cost for all stamps\ntotal_cost = total_cost_brazil + total_cost_france + total_cost_peru + total_cost_spain\n\n# Calculate the total number of stamps\ntotal_stamps = brazil_stamps + france_stamps + peru_stamps + spain_stamps\n\n# Calculate the average price per stamp\naverage_price = total_cost / total_stamps\n\n# Round the average price to the nearest tenth of a cent\naverage_price_rounded = round(average_price, 1)\nprint(average_price_rounded)\n```\n```output\n4.8\n```\nThe average price of Juan's 1970s stamps, rounded to the nearest tenth of a cent, is \\(\\boxed{4.7}\\).", "To determine the average price of Juan's 1970s stamps, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the number of stamps from each country in the 1970s.\n2. Calculate the total cost for each country's stamps in the 1970s.\