 y)\\) by \\(180^\\circ\\) counterclockwise about a point \\((a, b)\\) results in the point \\((2a - x, 2b - y)\\).\n   - So, the point \\((0,0)\\) rotated \\(180^\\circ\\) counterclockwise about \\((3,4)\\) becomes \\((2 \\cdot 3 - 0, 2 \\cdot 4 - 0) = (6, 8)\\).\n\nLet\'s implement this in Python to verify our results.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Part 1: Reflection over the vertical line x=1 and then over the line y=2\n# Initial point\nx1, y1 = 0, 0\n\n# Reflection over the vertical line x=1\nx2 = 2 - x1\ny2 = y1\n\n# Reflection over the line y=2\nx3 = x2\ny3 = 4 - y2\n\n# Part 2: Rotation of 180 degrees counterclockwise about the point (3,4)\n# Initial point\nx4, y4 = 0, 0\n# Point of rotation\na, b = 3, 4\n\n# Rotation of 180 degrees counterclockwise about (3,4)\nx5 = 2 * a - x4\ny5 = 2 * b - y4\n\n# Print the results\nprint(f"Part 1: ({x3}, {y3})")\nprint(f"Part 2: ({x5}, {y5})")\n```\n```output\nPart 1: (2, 4)\nPart 2: (6, 8)\n```\nThe results from the code execution confirm our reasoning. Therefore, the final answers are:\n\n1. The point \\((0,0)\\) is reflected over the vertical line \\(x=1\\) and then over the line \\(y=2\\), resulting in the point \\(\\boxed{(2, 4)}\\).\n2. The point \\((0,0)\\) is rotated \\(180^\\circ\\) counterclockwise about the point \\((3,4)\\), resulting in the point \\(\\boxed{(6, 8)}\\).', 'The point $(0,0)$ is rotated $90^\\circ$ clockwise about the origin.  When its image is then rotated $90^\\circ$ clockwise about the point $(1,0)$, what is the resulting point?\n\nWrite your answer in the form $(x, y)$ where $x$ and $y$ are real numbers.  \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \