\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\pi \\theta}{90} - 2 \\sin \\theta = \\frac{2\\pi}{3}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\pi \\theta - 180 \\sin \\theta = 60\\pi\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\theta - 180 \\frac{\\sin \\theta}{\\pi} = 60\n   \\]\n\nWe can solve this equation numerically using Python. Let's implement this and find the value of \\(\\theta\\).\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\ntheta = sp.symbols('theta')\n\n# Define the equation\nequation = sp.pi * theta / 90 - 2 * sp.sin(theta) - 2 * sp.pi / 3\n\n# Solve the equation\nsolution = sp.nsolve(equation, theta, 100)\n\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n100.000000000000\n```\nThe solution to the equation is \\(\\theta = 100^\\circ\\). Therefore, the measure of the smaller angle \\(\\angle ADC\\) is \\(\\boxed{100}\\) degrees.", 'The total area of the two circles is $\\pi(1^2) + \\pi(2^2) = 5\\pi$. The area of the shaded region is $\\frac{5}{12}$ of this, or $\\frac{25}{12}\\pi$. The area of the smaller circle is $\\pi$, so the area of the shaded region in the larger circle is $\\frac{25}{12}\\pi - \\pi = \\frac{13}{12}\\pi$.\n\nThe area of a sector of a circle is $\\frac{1}{2}r^2\\theta$, where $r$ is the radius and $\\theta$ is the central angle in radians. In this case, $r = 2$ and the area of the sector is $\\frac{13}{12}\\pi$. So we have:\n\n$$\\frac{1}{2}(2^2)\\theta = \\frac{13}{12}\\pi$$\n\n$$\\theta = \\frac{13}{12}\\pi$$\n\nTo convert radians to degrees, we multiply by $\\frac{180}{\\pi}$. So the measure of $\\angle ADC$ is:\n\n$$\\theta = \\frac{13}{12}\\pi \\cdot \\frac{180}{\\pi} = 195^\\circ$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of $\\angle ADC$ is $\\boxed{195^\\circ}$.', 'The area of the larger circle is $\\pi(2)^2 = 4\\pi$. The area of the smaller circle is $\\pi(1)^2 = \\pi$. The area of the shaded region is $\\frac5{12} \\cdot 4\\pi = \\frac{5\\pi}3$. The area of the smaller circle is $\\pi$, so the area of the shaded region is $\\frac{5\\pi}3 - \\pi = \\frac{2\\pi}3$. The area of the sector of the larger ci