ympy as sp\nfrom sympy.functions.combinatorial.numbers import binomial\n\n# Total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14 senators\ntotal_ways = binomial(14, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Republicans\nall_republicans = binomial(8, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Democrats\nall_democrats = binomial(6, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose 5 members with at least one member from each party\nat_least_one_from_each_party = total_ways - all_republicans - all_democrats\n\nprint(at_least_one_from_each_party)\n```\n```output\n1940\n```\nThe number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a group of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, ensuring that the subcommittee includes at least one member from each party, is \\(\\boxed{1940}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to find the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a group of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, where the subcommittee must have at least one member from each party.\n\nWe can break this problem down into manageable steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14 (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats):**\n   \\[\n   \\binom{14}{5}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Republicans:**\n   \\[\n   \\binom{8}{5}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Democrats:**\n   \\[\n   \\binom{6}{5}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Subtract the number of all-Republican and all-Democrat subcommittees from the total number of subcommittees to get the number of subcommittees with at least one member from each party:**\n   \\[\n   \\binom{14}{5} - \\binom{8}{5} - \\binom{6}{5}\n   \\]\n\nLet's implement this in Python using the `sympy` library:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the binomial coefficient function\ndef binomial(n, k):\n    return sp.binomial(n, k)\n\n# Total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14\ntotal_ways = binomial(14, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose 5 