4495\n```\nThe value of \\(\\dbinom{31}{28}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4495}\\).", 'To compute \\(\\binom{31}{28}\\), we can use the property of binomial coefficients that \\(\\binom{n}{k} = \\binom{n}{n-k}\\). Therefore, \\(\\binom{31}{28} = \\binom{31}{3}\\). The formula for a binomial coefficient is:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nSo, \\(\\binom{31}{3} = \\frac{31!}{3!(31-3)!} = \\frac{31!}{3! \\cdot 28!} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{26970}{6} = 4495\\).\n\nWe can confirm this using Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate binomial coefficient using math.comb which is available in Python 3.8+\nn = 31\nk = 28\n\n# Using the comb function to calculate binomial coefficient\nbinomial_coefficient = math.comb(n, k)\nprint(binomial_coefficient)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe value of \\(\\binom{31}{28}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4495}\\).', 'To compute $\\dbinom{31}{28}$, we can use the formula for combinations:\n\\[\n\\dbinom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\nwhere $n!$ denotes the factorial of $n$, which is the product of all positive integers up to $n$.\n\nFirst, we calculate the factorials:\n\\[\n31! = 31 \\times 30 \\times 29 \\times 28! \\\\\n28! = 28 \\times 27 \\times 26 \\times \\cdots \\times 1 \\\\\n3! = 3 \\times 2 \\times 1\n\\]\nNext, we substitute these values into the formula:\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31!}{28!3!} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29 \\times 28!}{28! \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1}\n\\]\nSince $28!$ appears in both the numerator and the denominator, we can cancel it out:\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}\n\\]\nNow, we can simplify the expression:\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{6} = 31 \\times 5 \\times 29 = 4495\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of $\\dbinom{31}{28}$ is $\\boxed{4495}$.', 'To compute \\(\\binom{31}{28}\\), we can use the formula for binomial coefficients:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, \\(n = 31\\) and \\(k = 28\\). Therefore:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{31}{28} = \\frac{31!}{28!(31-28)!} = \\frac{31!}{28! \\cdot 3!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this expression by canceling out the common factorial terms:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{31}{28} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29 \\times 28!}{28! \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{6}\n\\]\n\nNow we can calculate this step-by-step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Calculate the binomial coefficient using the formula\r\nfrom math import factorial\r\n\r\n# Given values\r\nn = 31\r\nk = 28\r\n\r\n# Calculate binomial coefficient\r\nbinom_coeff = factorial(n) // (factorial(k) * factorial(n - k))\r\nprint(binom_coeff)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe value of \\(\\binom{31}{28}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4495}\\).', "To solve the problem, we need to calculate the binomial coefficient $\\dbinom{31}{28}$. The binomial coefficient $\\dbinom{n}{k}$ is given by the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, $n = 31$ and $k = 28$. Therefore, we need to compute:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31!}{28!(31-28)!} = \\frac{31!}{28! \\cdot 3!}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the binomial coefficient\nn = 31\nk = 28\nbinomial_coefficient = math.comb(n, k)\nprint(binomial_coefficient)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe value of $\\dbinom{31}{28}$ is \\(\\boxed{4495}\\).", "To compute $\\dbinom{31}{28}$, we can use the formula for binomial coefficients:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, $n = 31$ and $k = 28$. So we have:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31!}{28!(31-28)!} = \\frac{31!}{28! \\cdot 3!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this expression by canceling out the common factorial terms in the numerator and the denominator. This leaves us with:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\