edian of the 27 consecutive integers is \\(a + 13 = 68 + 13 = 81\\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given sum of 27 consecutive integers\ntotal_sum = 3**7\n\n# Sum of the first 26 integers\nsum_first_26_integers = 26 * 27 // 2\n\n# Calculate the first integer 'a'\na = (total_sum - sum_first_26_integers) // 27\n\n# Calculate the median\nmedian = a + 13\nprint(median)\n```\n```output\n81\n```\nThe median of the 27 consecutive integers whose sum is \\(3^7\\) is \\(\\boxed{81}\\).", "To find the median of 27 consecutive positive integers whose sum is \\(3^7\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Let the 27 consecutive integers be \\(a, a+1, a+2, \\ldots, a+26\\).\n2. The sum of these integers can be expressed as:\n   \\[\n   a + (a+1) + (a+2) + \\cdots + (a+26)\n   \\]\n3. This sum can be simplified using the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Sum} = \\frac{n}{2} \\times (\\text{first term} + \\text{last term})\n   \\]\n   where \\(n\\) is the number of terms. In this case, \\(n = 27\\), the first term is \\(a\\), and the last term is \\(a+26\\). So the sum is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Sum} = \\frac{27}{2} \\times (a + (a + 26)) = \\frac{27}{2} \\times (2a + 26) = 27 \\times (a + 13)\n   \\]\n4. We are given that the sum is \\(3^7 = 2187\\). So we can set up the equation:\n   \\[\n   27 \\times (a + 13) = 2187\n   \\]\n5. Solving for \\(a\\):\n   \\[\n   a + 13 = \\frac{2187}{27} = 81\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   a = 81 - 13 = 68\n   \\]\n6. The median of 27 consecutive integers is the 14th term in the sequence. The 14th term is:\n   \\[\n   a + 13 = 68 + 13 = 81\n   \\]\n\nSo the median of the 27 consecutive integers is \\(81\\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given sum of 27 consecutive integers\ntotal_sum = 3**7\n\n# Number of integers\nn = 27\n\n# Calculate the first term 'a'\na = (total_sum // n) - 13\n\n# Calculate the median (14th term)\nmedian = a + 13\nprint(median)\n`