on by multiplying their hourly wage in US dollars by 8.\n5. Compare the daily earnings to determine who earns the most.\n\nLet\'s perform these calculations using Python.\n```python\n# Given data\nnavin_hourly_wage_rupees = 160\nluka_hourly_wage_kuna = 25\nian_hourly_wage_pula = 34\n\n# Conversion rates\nusd_to_rupees = 32.35\nusd_to_kuna = 5.18\nusd_to_pula = 6.95\n\n# Convert hourly wages to US dollars\nnavin_hourly_wage_usd = navin_hourly_wage_rupees / usd_to_rupees\nluka_hourly_wage_usd = luka_hourly_wage_kuna / usd_to_kuna\nian_hourly_wage_usd = ian_hourly_wage_pula / usd_to_pula\n\n# Calculate daily earnings (8 hours a day)\nnavin_daily_earnings_usd = navin_hourly_wage_usd * 8\nluka_daily_earnings_usd = luka_hourly_wage_usd * 8\nian_daily_earnings_usd = ian_hourly_wage_usd * 8\n\n# Determine who earns the most\nearnings = {\n    "Navin": navin_daily_earnings_usd,\n    "Luka": luka_daily_earnings_usd,\n    "Ian": ian_daily_earnings_usd\n}\n\nmax_earner = max(earnings, key=earnings.get)\nmax_earnings = earnings[max_earner]\n\nprint((max_earner, max_earnings))\n```\n```output\n(\'Navin\', 39.63133047210301)\n```\nAfter performing the calculations, we find that Navin earns the most after working an eight-hour day. His daily earnings are approximately $39.63.\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Navin}}\n\\]', 'To determine who earns the most after working an eight-hour day, we need to convert the hourly wages of Navin, Luka, and Ian into a common currency, such as US dollars. We will use the given exchange rates to convert their wages into US dollars.\n\nHere are the steps:\n\n1. Convert Navin\'s hourly wage from rupees to US dollars.\n2. Convert Luka\'s hourly wage from kuna to US dollars.\n3. Convert Ian\'s hourly wage from pula to US dollars.\n4. Calculate the daily earnings for each person by multiplying their hourly wage in US dollars by 8 hours.\n5. Compare the daily earnings to determine who earns the most.\n\nLet\'s perform these calculations u