lculate the sum of the coefficients of g(x) by evaluating g(1)\nsum_of_coefficients = g(1)\nprint(sum_of_coefficients)\n```", "To find the sum of the coefficients of the polynomial \\(g(x) = f(x-1)\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Define the polynomial \\(f(x) = 3x^4 + 5x^2 - 9x - 2\\).\n2. Substitute \\(x-1\\) into \\(f(x)\\) to get \\(g(x) = f(x-1)\\).\n3. Expand the polynomial \\(g(x)\\).\n4. Find the sum of the coefficients of \\(g(x)\\).\n\nThe sum of the coefficients of a polynomial \\(P(x)\\) is equal to \\(P(1)\\). So, we need to evaluate \\(g(1) = f(1-1) = f(0)\\).\n\nLet's implement this in Python using sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nx = sp.symbols('x')\n\n# Define the polynomial f(x)\nf = 3*x**4 + 5*x**2 - 9*x - 2\n\n# Substitute x-1 into f(x) to get g(x)\ng = f.subs(x, x-1)\n\n# Expand the polynomial g(x)\ng_expanded = sp.expand(g)\n\n# Find the sum of the coefficients of g(x), which is g(1)\nsum_of_coefficients = g_expanded.subs(x, 1)\n\nprint(sum_of_coefficients)\n```\n```output\n-9\n```\nThe sum of the coefficients of the polynomial \\(g(x) = f(x-1)\\) is \\(\\boxed{-9}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to find the polynomial \\(g(x) = f(x-1)\\) and then compute the sum of its coefficients. The sum of the coefficients of a polynomial \\(p(x)\\) is equal to \\(p(1)\\). So, we need to evaluate \\(g(1)\\), which is \\(f(1-1) = f(0)\\).\n\nLet's break it down step-by-step:\n\n1. Define the polynomial \\(f(x) = 3x^4 + 5x^2 - 9x - 2\\).\n2. Substitute \\(x = 0\\) into \\(f(x)\\) to find \\(f(0)\\).\n3. The result will be the sum of the coefficients of \\(g(x)\\).\n\nLet's implement this in Python using sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable and the polynomial f(x)\nx = sp.symbols('x')\nf = 3*x**4 + 5*x**2 - 9*x - 2\n\n# Substitute x = 0 into f(x) to find the sum of the coefficients of g(x)\nsum_of_coefficients = f.subs(x, 0)\nprint(sum_of_coefficients)\n```\n```output\n-2\n```\nThe sum of 