 ensure accuracy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variables\nx, y, x1, y1, x2, y2 = sp.symbols('x y x1 y1 x2 y2')\n\n# Equation of the tangent to the circle at (x1, y1)\ntangent_circle = x*x1 + y*y1 - 2\n\n# Equation of the tangent to the parabola at (x2, y2)\ntangent_parabola = y*y2 - 4*(x + x2)\n\n# Since these are the same line, we can equate the coefficients\n# We need to solve for x1, y1, x2, y2\n# We know y2^2 = 8*x2, so we can substitute y2 = sqrt(8*x2) or y2 = -sqrt(8*x2)\n\n# Let's solve for y2 = sqrt(8*x2)\ny2_positive = sp.sqrt(8*x2)\ntangent_parabola_positive = tangent_parabola.subs(y2, y2_positive)\n\n# Equate the coefficients of x and y\ncoeff_x_circle = x1\ncoeff_y_circle = y1\nconstant_circle = -2\n\ncoeff_x_parabola_positive = -4\ncoeff_y_parabola_positive = y2_positive\nconstant_parabola_positive = -4*x2\n\n# Set up the equations\neq1 = sp.Eq(coeff_x_circle, coeff_x_parabola_positive)\neq2 = sp.Eq(coeff_y_circle, coeff_y_parabola_positive)\neq3 = sp.Eq(constant_circle, constant_parabola_positive)\n\n# Solve the equations\nsolution_positive = sp.solve([eq1, eq2, eq3], (x1, y1, x2))\n\n# Now let's solve for y2 = -sqrt(8*x2)\ny2_negative = -sp.sqrt(8*x2)\ntangent_parabola_negative = tangent_parabola.subs(y2, y2_negative)\n\n# Equate the coefficients of x and y\ncoeff_x_parabola_negative = -4\ncoeff_y_parabola_negative = y2_negative\nconstant_parabola_negative = -4*x2\n\n# Set up the equations\neq1 = sp.Eq(coeff_x_circle, coeff_x_parabola_negative)\neq2 = sp.Eq(coeff_y_circle, coeff_y_parabola_negative)\neq3 = sp.Eq(constant_circle, constant_parabola_negative)\n\n# Solve the equations\nsolution_negative = sp.solve([eq1, eq2, eq3], (x1, y1, x2))\n\n# Combine the solutions\nsolutions = [solution_positive, solution_negative]\nprint(solutions)\n```\n```output\n[[(-4, -4*sqrt(2*x2), x2), (-4, 4*sqrt(2*x2), x2)], [(-4, -4*sqrt(2*x2), x2), (-4, 4*sqrt(2*x2), x2)]]\n```\nFrom the output, we see that the solutions for the points of tangency are