al answer is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to evaluate the function \\(f(n)\\) for three different values: \\(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\), \\(\\sqrt{45}\\), and \\(8^{2/3}\\). We will then sum the results of these evaluations.\n\nThe function \\(f(n)\\) is defined as:\n\\[f(n) = \\left\\{\n\\begin{array}{cl}\n\\lfloor n \\rfloor & \\text{ if }n \\geq 4, \\\\\n\\lceil n \\rceil & \\text{ if } n < 4.\n\\end{array}\n\\right.\\]\n\nLet's evaluate each term separately:\n\n1. Evaluate \\(f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)\\):\n   - \\(\\frac{\\pi}{3} \\approx 1.047\\), which is less than 4.\n   - So, \\(f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\lceil \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\rceil = \\lceil 1.047 \\rceil = 2\\).\n\n2. Evaluate \\(f(\\sqrt{45})\\):\n   - \\(\\sqrt{45} \\approx 6.708\\), which is greater than or equal to 4.\n   - So, \\(f(\\sqrt{45}) = \\lfloor \\sqrt{45} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 6.708 \\rfloor = 6\\).\n\n3. Evaluate \\(f(8^{2/3})\\):\n   - \\(8^{2/3} = (2^3)^{2/3} = 2^2 = 4\\), which is equal to 4.\n   - So, \\(f(8^{2/3}) = \\lfloor 4 \\rfloor = 4\\).\n\nNow, we sum the results:\n\\[f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) + f(\\sqrt{45}) + f(8^{2/3}) = 2 + 6 + 4 = 12.\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\r\n\r\n# Define the function f(n)\r\ndef f(n):\r\n    if n >= 4:\r\n        return math.floor(n)\r\n    else:\r\n        return math.ceil(n)\r\n\r\n# Evaluate f(pi/3)\r\npi_over_3 = math.pi / 3\r\nf_pi_over_3 = f(pi_over_3)\r\n\r\n# Evaluate f(sqrt(45))\r\nsqrt_45 = math.sqrt(45)\r\nf_sqrt_45 = f(sqrt_45)\r\n\r\n# Evaluate f(8^(2/3))\r\neight_two_thirds = 8 ** (2 / 3)\r\nf_eight_two_thirds = f(eight_two_thirds)\r\n\r\n# Sum the results\r\nresult = f_pi_over_3 + f_sqrt_45 + f_eight_two_thirds\r\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to evaluate the function \\(f(n)\\) for three different values: \\(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\), \\(\\sqrt{45}\\), and \\(8^{2/3}\\). The function \\(