 speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance)\nfractional_part = distance - whole_number\nfraction_numerator = int(fractional_part * 2)  # since the fractional part is in halves\n\n# Display the result as a mixed number\nmixed_number = f"{whole_number} {fraction_numerator}/2"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(\\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours at a constant speed of 50 miles per hour.', 'To find out how far a car travels at a constant speed of 50 miles per hour in \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nHere, the speed is 50 miles per hour, and the time is \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, which is equivalent to \\(2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4}\\) hours.\n\nSo, the distance traveled is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} = \\frac{275}{2} \\]\n\nTo express \\(\\frac{275}{2}\\) as a mixed number, we divide 275 by 2 to get the whole number part and the remainder:\n\n\\[ 275 \\div 2 = 137 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\]\n\nSo, \\(\\frac{275}{2} = 137\\frac{1}{2}\\).\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nnumerator = int(fractional_part * 2)  # since the denominator is 2\n\nmixed_number = f"{whole_number} {numerator}/2" if numerator != 0 else f"{whole_number}"\n\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(\\boxed{137\\frac{1}{2}}\\) miles in \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours at a constant speed of 50 miles per hour.', "To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour for \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) 