,2)$ is $\\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{18}$.\nThe probability of rolling $(3,4)$ or $(4,3)$ is $\\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{18}$.\n\nSo the total probability of rolling a sum of 7 is:\n\\[ 2pq + \\frac{1}{18} + \\frac{1}{18} = \\frac{47}{288} \\]\n\\[ 2pq + \\frac{1}{9} = \\frac{47}{288} \\]\n\\[ 2pq = \\frac{47}{288} - \\frac{1}{9} \\]\n\\[ 2pq = \\frac{47}{288} - \\frac{32}{288} \\]\n\\[ 2pq = \\frac{15}{288} \\]\n\\[ 2pq = \\frac{5}{96} \\]\n\\[ pq = \\frac{5}{192} \\]\nSince $p + q = \\frac{1}{3}$, we can solve for $p$ and $q$ by substituting $q = \\frac{1}{3} - p$ into the equation $pq = \\frac{5}{192}$:\n\\[ p \\left( \\frac{1}{3} - p \\right) = \\frac{5}{192} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{p}{3} - p^2 = \\frac{5}{192} \\]\n\\[ 64p - 192p^2 = 5 \\]\n\\[ 192p^2 - 64p + 5 = 0 \\]\nWe can solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula $p = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}$, where $a = 192$, $b = -64$, and $c = 5$:\n\\[ p = \\frac{64 \\pm \\sqrt{64^2 - 4 \\cdot 192 \\cdot 5}}{2 \\cdot 192} \\]\n\\[ p = \\frac{64 \\pm \\sqrt{4096 - 3840}}{384} \\]\n\\[ p = \\frac{64 \\pm \\sqrt{256}}{384} \\]\n\\[ p = \\frac{64 \\pm 16}{384} \\]\nThis gives us two solutions:\n\\[ p = \\frac{80}{384} = \\frac{5}{24} \\]\n\\[ p = \\frac{48}{384} = \\frac{1}{8} \\]\nSince $\\frac{1}{6} < p < \\frac{1}{3}$, the valid solution is $p = \\frac{5}{24}$. Therefore, the probability of obtaining face $F$ is $\\frac{5}{24}$, and the sum $m+n$ is $5+24=29$. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\r\n\r\n# Define the variables\r\np, q = symbols('p q')\r\n\r\n# Define the equations\r\neq1 = Eq(p + q, 1/3)\r\neq2 = Eq(p * q, 5/192)\r\n\r\n# Solve the system of equations\r\nsolution = solve((eq1, eq2), (p, q))\r\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n[(0.208333333333333, 0.166666666666667), (0.166666666666667, 0.208333333333333)]\n```\nThe solutions to the 