 cube's side length is the diameter of the sphere, which is 2 * 3 = 6 inches. The volume of the cube is 6^3 = 216 cubic inches. \\boxed{216}\n\n2. A steel sphere with a 3-inch radius is made by removing metal from the corners of a cube that has the shortest possible side lengths. How many cubic inches are in the volume of the sphere? \\boxed{36π}\n\n3. A steel sphere with a 3-inch radius is made by removing metal from the corners of a cube that has the shortest possible side lengths. How many cubic inches are in the volume of the metal removed from the cube? \\boxed{180}", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the side length of the cube from which a steel sphere with a 3-inch radius is made by removing metal from the corners of the cube. The sphere is inscribed within the cube, meaning the diameter of the sphere is equal to the side length of the cube.\n\n1. The radius of the sphere is 3 inches, so the diameter of the sphere is \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\) inches.\n2. Since the sphere is inscribed in the cube, the side length of the cube is equal to the diameter of the sphere, which is 6 inches.\n3. The volume of the cube can be calculated using the formula for the volume of a cube, \\(V = s^3\\), where \\(s\\) is the side length of the cube.\n\nLet's calculate the volume of the cube using Python code.\n```python\n# Side length of the cube\nside_length = 6\n\n# Volume of the cube\nvolume_cube = side_length ** 3\nprint(volume_cube)\n```\n```output\n216\n```\nThe volume of the cube is \\(\\boxed{216}\\) cubic inches.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the side length of the cube from which the steel sphere is made. The sphere is inscribed within the cube, meaning that the diameter of the sphere is equal to the side length of the cube. Given that the radius of the sphere is 3 inches, the diameter of the sphere (which is twice the radius) is \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\) inches. Therefore, the side length of the cube is 6 inches.\n\nThe volume \\(V\\) of a cube with side length \\(s\\) is given by the formula \\(V = s^3\\). In this case, the side length \\(s\\) is 6 inches. So, the volume of the cube is \\(6^3 = 216\\) cubic inches.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given radius of the sphere\nradius_sphere = 3\n\n# Diameter of the sphere (which is the side length of the cube)\nside_length_cube = 2 * radius_sphere\n\n# Volume of the cube\nvolume_cube = side_length_cube ** 3\nprint(volume_cube)\n```\n```output\n216\n```\nThe volume of the cube is \\(\\boxed{216}\\) cubic inches.", 'The volume of a sphere is given by the formula \\( V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3 \\). For a sphere with a radius of 3 inches, the volume is:\n\\[ V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (3)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\cdot 27 = 36\\pi \\text{ cubic inches} \\]\n\nThe volume of the cube is the volume of the sphere plus the volume of the metal removed from the corners of the cube. Since the sphere is made by removing metal from the corners of the cube, the diameter of the sphere is equal to the side length of the cube. The diameter of the sphere is \\( 2 \\times 3 = 6 \\) inches, so the side length of the cube is 6 inches. The volume of the cube is:\n\\[ V_{\\text{cube}} = 6^3 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches} \\]\n\nThe volume of the metal removed from the corners of the cube is the volume of the cube minus the volume of the sphere:\n\\[ V_{\\text{removed}} = V_{\\text{cube}} - V_{\\text{sphere}} = 216 - 36\\pi \\text{ cubic inches} \\]\n\nTherefore, the volume of the cube is \\( \\boxed{216} \\) cubic inches.\n\nA steel sphere with a 3-inch radius is made by removing metal from the corners of a cube that has the shortest possible side lengths. What percent of the volume of the cube is the volume of the sphere? \\boxed{ \\text{percentage} }\nThe volume of the sphere is \\( 36\\pi \\) cubic inches, and the volume of the cube is 216 cubic inches. The percentage of the volume of the cube that is the volume of the sphere is:\n\\[ \\text{percentage} = \\left( \\frac{36\\pi}{216} \\right) \\times 100 = \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right) \\times 100 \\approx 52.36\\% \\]\n\nTherefore, the percentage of the volume of the cube that is the volume of the sphere is \\( \\boxed{52.36\\%} \\).\n\nA steel sphere with a 3-inch radius is made by removing metal from the corners of a cube that has the shortest possible side lengths. How many cubic inches are in the volume of the metal that was removed from the cube? \\boxed{ \\text{volume of metal removed} }\nThe volume of the metal removed from the cube is the volume of the cube minus the volume of the sphere:\n\\[ V_{\\text{removed}} = V_{\\text{cube}} - V_{\\text{sphere}} = 216 - 36\\pi \\text{ cubic inches} \\]\n\nTherefore, the volume of the metal that was removed from the cube is \\( \\boxed{216 - 36\\pi} \\) cubic inches.\n\nA steel sphere with a 3-inch radius is made by removing metal from the corners of a cube that has the shortest possible side lengths. What is the ratio of the volume of the sphere to the volume of the cube? \\boxed{ \\text{ratio} }\nThe volume of the sphere is \\( 36\\pi \\) cubic inches, and the volume of the cube is 216 cubic inches. The ratio of the volume of the sphere to the volume of the cube is:\n\\[ \\text{ratio} = \\frac{36\\pi}{216} = \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\]\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the volume of the sphere to the volume of the cube is \\( \\boxed{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\).\n\nA steel sphere with a 3-inch radius is made by removing metal from the corners of a cube that has the shortest possible side lengths. How many cubic inches are in the volume of the sphere? \\boxed{ \\text{volume of sphere} }\nThe volume of the sphere is given by the formula \\( V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3 \\). For a sphere with a radius of 3 inches, the volume is:\n\\[ V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (3)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\cdot 27 = 36\\pi \\text{ cubic inches} \\]\n\nTherefore, the volume of the sphere is \\( \\boxed{36\\pi} \\) cubic inches.\n\nA steel sphere with a 3-inch radius is made by remo