es for each part\nhairstyles = 4  # 3 hairstyles + bald\neyebrows = 2\nears = 2\nlips = 2\neyes = 1\nshoes = 2\n\n# Total number of different personalities\ntotal_personalities = hairstyles * eyebrows * ears * lips * eyes * shoes\nprint(total_personalities)\n```\n```output\n64\n```\nThe total number of different wacky personalities Tom can come up with is \\(\\boxed{64}\\).", "To determine the total number of different personalities Tom can create for his Mr. Potato Head, we need to consider the number of choices for each attribute. Since Tom can choose from 3 hairstyles (including bald), 2 sets of eyebrows, 1 pair of googly eyes, 2 sets of ears, 2 sets of lips, and 2 pairs of shoes, we can calculate the total number of different personalities by multiplying the number of choices for each attribute together.\n\nThe calculation is as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total Personalities} = (\\text{Number of hairstyles}) \\times (\\text{Number of eyebrow sets}) \\times (\\text{Number of eye pairs}) \\times (\\text{Number of ear sets}) \\times (\\text{Number of lip sets}) \\times (\\text{Number of shoe pairs})\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total Personalities} = 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Number of choices for each attribute\nnum_hairstyles = 3\nnum_eyebrow_sets = 2\nnum_eye_pairs = 1\nnum_ear_sets = 2\nnum_lip_sets = 2\nnum_shoe_pairs = 2\n\n# Calculate the total number of different personalities\ntotal_personalities = num_hairstyles * num_eyebrow_sets * num_eye_pairs * num_ear_sets * num_lip_sets * num_shoe_pairs\nprint(total_personalities)\n```\n```output\n48\n```\nThe total number of different wacky personalities Tom can come up with for his Mr. Potato Head is \\(\\boxed{48}\\).", "To determine the number of different wacky personalities Tom can come up with, we need to consider each of the optional components (hair, eyebrows, ears, lips, and shoes) and calculate the total number of co